## 📋 Prerequisites

Before running the script, ensure:

- Ubuntu-based Linux system
- Git installed
- Internet connection
- Sudo privileges

---

## ⚙️ Installation

Clone this repository

```bash
git clone <your-repository-url>
cd <repository-name>
```

Give execute permission

```bash
chmod +x deploy.sh
```

Run the script

```bash
./deploy.sh
```

---

## 🔄 Deployment Workflow

The script performs the following operations:

### 1. Clone Repository

Checks whether the project directory already exists.

If it doesn't exist, clones the Django Notes App from GitHub.

---

### 2. Install Dependencies

Installs:

- Docker
- Docker Compose
- Nginx

using

```bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y nginx docker.io docker-compose
```

---

### 3. Configure Services

- Changes Docker socket ownership
- Enables Docker service
- Enables Nginx service
- Restarts Docker

---

### 4. Deploy Application

Builds the Docker image

```bash
docker build -t notes-app .
```

Starts containers

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

---

